  "summary": "global/country-language-mismatch — PWA Component",
  "description": "As a Developer, \n\nI want a reusable global/country-language-mismatch React component built to the Zimmermann Design System 2026 spec, \n\nso that it can be consumed across storefronts to surface country and language mismatch prompts to shoppers in a consistent drawer pattern.\n\n----\n\nThe component covers two variants, both rendered as a right-anchored drawer panel using the shared drawer shell:\n\nLocation Prompt Banner: displayed when the shopper's IP-detected country does not match the current storefront (consumed by [SFCC-823](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-823) )\n\nLanguage Prompt Banner: displayed when the shopper's browser language does not match the current EU storefront locale (consumed by [SFCC-689](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-689))\n\nThe component does not own the trigger logic or redirect behaviour — that is handled by the consuming stories. It exposes callbacks for each CTA action and accepts props to control which variant renders.",
  "status": {
    "name": "Tech design",
    "category": "To Do",
    "color": "blue-gray"
  },
