    "value": "Shared shell behaviour\n\n1. Given the component is rendered in either variant, when it opens, then it slides in as a right-anchored drawer — full width on mobile with space at the bottom — per Figma design specs.\n2. Given the drawer is open, when the shopper taps or clicks the backdrop or close icon, then the drawer closes without firing any CTA callback.\n3. Given the component is rendered, when a keyboard user interacts with the drawer, then focus is trapped within the open drawer, all interactive elements are reachable via keyboard, and closing the drawer returns focus to the trigger element.\n4. Given the component is rendered, when a screen reader user interacts, then the drawer is announced as a dialog with an accessible name matching the active variant, all CTAs have descriptive labels, and the close icon has an aria-label.\n\nLocation Prompt Banner variant\n\n5. Given the component renders with variant=location-prompt, when the drawer opens, then it displays the shopper's detected country, a message indicating a mismatch with the current storefront, and two CTAs: one to redirect to the correct storefront and one to stay on the current storefront.\n6. Given the location prompt variant is rendered, when the shopper confirms the redirect CTA, then onRedirect() fires and the consuming page handles navigation.\n7. Given the location prompt variant is rendered, when the shopper selects stay on current storefront, then the drawer closes without firing a redirect callback.\n\nLanguage Prompt Banner variant\n\n8. Given the component renders with variant=language-prompt, when the drawer opens, then it displays the detected browser language, the current storefront locale, and two CTAs: one to switch to the matched language and one to stay in the current language.\n9. Given the language prompt variant is rendered, when the shopper confirms the language switch CTA, then onSwitchLanguage(locale) fires with the target locale and the consuming page handles the redirect.\n10. Given the language prompt variant is rendered, when the shopper selects stay in current language, then onDismiss() fires and the drawer closes."
  }
